From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:10:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): xhttp transport with sing-box-extended

Build-If: variant=homeproxy sb=extended

The xhttp transport of Xray is in sing-box-extended and podkop-engine,
not in the official sing-box. Support it where the core has it:

- homeproxy.uc and rpcd: singBoxHasXHTTP() / hp_has_xhttp ask the core
  with "sing-box check" of a one outbound config; the build tags do not
  tell. The answer is cached per binary (size and mtime), so a core
  replaced by apk is asked again.
- node.js: XHTTP in the transport list with host, path, mode, padding
  and "extra settings": the extra JSON of an Xray link (headers, xmux,
  downloadSettings and the rest). Without a core that has xhttp the
  entry says so and a node with it cannot be saved.
- Subscriptions and the share link import: xhttp and splithttp links
  are read (host, path, mode, extra as JSON or base64, x_padding_bytes
  of 3x-ui) when the core has xhttp, otherwise skipped as before.
- generate_client.uc: the node becomes an xhttp transport. Extra is
  mapped to the sing-box names (with the old session names and
  downloadSettings with TLS or REALITY), Host moves out of the headers
  (sing-box refuses it there), zero ranges mean the default and the
  padding is never empty ("x_padding_bytes cannot be disabled"). An
  unknown or invalid extra is reported in the log and left out.
- xhttp is added to the transports that patch 015 lets through only
  when the core has it. With another core (e.g. the official sing-box
  after apk upgrade) such a node becomes a block outbound with a log
  line, as any transport this homeproxy does not know: its traffic is
  dropped instead of the whole configuration being refused, and it is
  never sent direct.
- A mode of Re:HomeProxy's core (bidi, packet-down, stream-down) is
  reported in the log and becomes auto.
- The log lines of the generator carry the time and [DAEMON], like the
  rest of the homeproxy log.

Without xhttp nodes the generated configuration is byte-identical to
before (7 test configurations, sing-box 1.14.2 and
1.14.1-extended-2.7.2).

Checked: share links of vless, trojan and vmess with xhttp, splithttp,
extra as JSON and base64, an invalid extra, through the real parse_uri
and parseShareLink, then the generator and "sing-box check" on both
cores (also custom routing with bind_interface, detour and
domain_resolver, and a URLTest group); a live loopback with
sing-box-extended as the xhttp server and the generated outbound as the
client: auto, packet-up, stream-up and stream-one, plain and over TLS,
3 MB files byte-identical, three parallel downloads, extra with headers,
xmux, padding and sc_max_each_post_bytes.

The mode auto is resolved as Xray does it: stream-one with REALITY
(stream-up with downloadSettings), packet-up otherwise. sing-box-extended
takes packet-up for auto, and a REALITY server set to stream-one or
stream-up refuses it ("packet-up mode is not allowed"): share links of
such servers say auto, so every request timed out after 15 s ("context
deadline exceeded") while Xray clients worked. Checked live against
Xray 26.10.10 with the server in each mode.

Without an xmux in the extra (share links usually have none) the
defaults of Xray are taken: max_connections 3, h_max_request_times
600-900, h_max_reusable_secs 1800-3000. sing-box-extended has no such
defaults and opens a TCP and TLS connection for every proxied
connection, so 20 parallel requests made 20 REALITY handshakes. A node
of 3x-ui timed out that way while Xray clients with the same link
worked, and worked once the xmux was set. With the defaults 20 parallel
requests go over 3 connections, an xmux of the link (also inside
downloadSettings) replaces them, and after a restart of the server the
node answers again within a second (checked live against Xray
26.10.10).

sing-box-extended 2.7.3 checks a sessionIDTable as Xray does (an ASCII
table, sessionIDLength from 1, at least 2^31 IDs) and refuses the whole
configuration otherwise, where 2.7.2 took it. Such a table, and a
maxConcurrency next to a maxConnections (refused by both), are now left
out with a log line, so one bad node of a subscription does not stop
homeproxy; without a table the session ID is a UUID, as in Xray. Checked
on 2.7.2 and 2.7.3 with hex/7 (refused by Xray), hex/8, hex/7-8, a
custom table, a non-ASCII table, a table without a length, both xmux
limits and a bad table inside downloadSettings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011cyCFAA9hPeqN8wsgkxbrJ
---
diff --git a/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/homeproxy/node.js b/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/homeproxy/node.js
index de350bc..3648b87 100644
--- a/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/homeproxy/node.js
+++ b/htdocs/luci-static/resources/view/homeproxy/node.js
@@ -23,14 +23,44 @@ function allowInsecureConfirm(ev, _section_id, value) {
  * ...) would make sing-box reject the whole configuration, so such a link is
  * not imported. "raw" is the newer Xray name of plain TCP. */
 const supported_transports = ['grpc', 'h2', 'http', 'httpupgrade', 'quic', 'ws'];
+const xhttp_modes = ['auto', 'packet-up', 'stream-up', 'stream-one'];
 
+/* splithttp is the old name of xhttp */
 function transportType(type) {
-	return (!type || ['tcp', 'raw'].includes(type)) ? null : type;
+	if (!type || ['tcp', 'raw'].includes(type))
+		return null;
+
+	return (type === 'splithttp') ? 'xhttp' : type;
 }
 
-function unsupportedTransport(type) {
+/* xhttp needs a core that has it (sing-box-extended, podkop-engine) */
+function unsupportedTransport(type, features) {
 	type = transportType(type);
-	return !!type && !supported_transports.includes(type);
+	return !!type && !supported_transports.includes(type) &&
+		!(type === 'xhttp' && features && features.hp_has_xhttp);
+}
+
+/* A share link carries XHTTP as Xray does: the host, the path and the mode as
+ * parameters, the rest as JSON in "extra" (3x-ui also repeats the padding as
+ * x_padding_bytes). The generator turns extra into sing-box options. */
+function parseXHTTP(config, params) {
+	config.xhttp_host = params.get('host') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('host')) : null;
+	config.http_path = params.get('path') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('path')) : null;
+	config.xhttp_mode = xhttp_modes.includes(params.get('mode')) ? params.get('mode') : null;
+	config.xhttp_padding_bytes = params.get('x_padding_bytes');
+
+	let extra = (params.get('extra') || '').trim();
+	if (extra) {
+		try {
+			if (!extra.startsWith('{'))
+				extra = hp.decodeBase64Str(extra);
+			extra = JSON.parse(extra);
+			if (extra && typeof extra === 'object' && !Array.isArray(extra))
+				config.xhttp_extra = JSON.stringify(extra);
+		} catch(e) {
+			/* An invalid extra is left out, as by the subscriptions */
+		}
+	}
 }
 
 function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
@@ -218,7 +248,7 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 			if (!url.username)
 				return null;
 			/* Unsupported transport */
-			else if (unsupportedTransport(params.get('type')))
+			else if (unsupportedTransport(params.get('type'), features))
 				return null;
 
 			config = {
@@ -244,6 +274,10 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 					config.ws_path = config.ws_path.split('?ed=')[0];
 				}
 				break;
+			case 'xhttp':
+			case 'splithttp':
+				parseXHTTP(config, params);
+				break;
 			}
 
 			break;
@@ -277,7 +311,7 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 			params = url.searchParams;
 
 			/* Unsupported transport */
-			if (unsupportedTransport(params.get('type')))
+			if (unsupportedTransport(params.get('type'), features))
 				return null;
 			else if (params.get('type') === 'quic' && ((params.get('quicSecurity') && params.get('quicSecurity') !== 'none') || !features.with_quic))
 				return null;
@@ -317,6 +351,10 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 				config.httpupgrade_host = params.get('host') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('host')) : null;
 				config.http_path = params.get('path') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('path')) : null;
 				break;
+			case 'xhttp':
+			case 'splithttp':
+				parseXHTTP(config, params);
+				break;
 			case 'ws':
 				config.ws_host = params.get('host') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('host')) : null;
 				config.ws_path = params.get('path') ? decodeURIComponent(params.get('path')) : null;
@@ -340,7 +378,7 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 			if (uri.v != '2')
 				return null;
 			/* Unsupported transports */
-			else if (unsupportedTransport(uri.net))
+			else if (unsupportedTransport(uri.net, features))
 				return null;
 			else if (uri.net === 'quic' && ((uri.type && uri.type !== 'none') || !features.with_quic))
 				return null;
@@ -380,6 +418,13 @@ function parseShareLink(uri, features) {
 				config.httpupgrade_host = uri.host;
 				config.http_path = uri.path;
 				break;
+			case 'xhttp':
+			case 'splithttp':
+				/* v2rayN writes the mode as the header type */
+				config.xhttp_host = uri.host;
+				config.http_path = uri.path;
+				config.xhttp_mode = xhttp_modes.includes(uri.type) ? uri.type : null;
+				break;
 			case 'ws':
 				config.ws_host = uri.host;
 				config.ws_path = uri.path;
@@ -797,15 +842,24 @@ function renderNodeSettings(section, data, features, main_node, routing_mode) {
 	o.value('httpupgrade', _('HTTPUpgrade'));
 	o.value('quic', _('QUIC'));
 	o.value('ws', _('WebSocket'));
+	o.value('xhttp', features.hp_has_xhttp ? _('XHTTP') : _('XHTTP (not supported by this sing-box)'));
 	o.depends('type', 'trojan');
 	o.depends('type', 'vless');
 	o.depends('type', 'vmess');
+	o.validate = function(section_id, value) {
+		if (value === 'xhttp' && !features.hp_has_xhttp)
+			return _('The installed sing-box has no XHTTP transport: install sing-box-extended or choose another transport.');
+
+		return true;
+	}
 	o.onchange = function(ev, section_id, value) {
 		let desc = this.map.findElement('id', 'cbid.homeproxy.%s.transport'.format(section_id)).nextElementSibling;
 		if (value === 'http')
 			desc.innerHTML = _('TLS is not enforced. If TLS is not configured, plain HTTP 1.1 is used.');
 		else if (value === 'quic')
 			desc.innerHTML = _('No additional encryption support: It\'s basically duplicate encryption.');
+		else if (value === 'xhttp')
+			desc.innerHTML = _('XHTTP of Xray. Needs sing-box-extended or podkop-engine.');
 		else
 			desc.innerHTML = _('No TCP transport, plain HTTP is merged into the HTTP transport.');
 
@@ -855,6 +909,7 @@ function renderNodeSettings(section, data, features, main_node, routing_mode) {
 	o = s.option(form.Value, 'http_path', _('Path'));
 	o.depends('transport', 'http');
 	o.depends('transport', 'httpupgrade');
+	o.depends('transport', 'xhttp');
 	o.modalonly = true;
 
 	o = s.option(form.Value, 'http_method', _('Method'));
@@ -902,6 +957,53 @@ function renderNodeSettings(section, data, features, main_node, routing_mode) {
 	o.modalonly = true;
 	/* WebSocket config end */
 
+	/* XHTTP config start */
+	o = s.option(form.Value, 'xhttp_host', _('Host'));
+	o.datatype = 'hostname';
+	o.depends('transport', 'xhttp');
+	o.modalonly = true;
+
+	o = s.option(form.ListValue, 'xhttp_mode', _('XHTTP mode'),
+		_('<code>auto</code>: <code>stream-one</code> with REALITY (<code>stream-up</code> with a download server), <code>packet-up</code> otherwise.'));
+	o.value('', _('Default'));
+	xhttp_modes.forEach((m) => o.value(m, m));
+	o.depends('transport', 'xhttp');
+	o.modalonly = true;
+
+	o = s.option(form.Value, 'xhttp_padding_bytes', _('Padding bytes'),
+		_('A range of padding in each request, e.g. <code>100-1000</code> (the default).'));
+	o.placeholder = '100-1000';
+	o.validate = function(section_id, value) {
+		if (value && !/^\d+(-\d+)?$/.test(value))
+			return _('Expecting: %s').format(_('a number or a range like 100-1000'));
+
+		return true;
+	}
+	o.depends('transport', 'xhttp');
+	o.modalonly = true;
+
+	o = s.option(form.TextValue, 'xhttp_extra', _('Extra settings'),
+		_('The <code>extra</code> JSON of an Xray XHTTP link: headers, xmux, downloadSettings and other settings. Host, path and mode above take precedence.'));
+	o.rows = 6;
+	o.monospace = true;
+	o.validate = function(section_id, value) {
+		if (!value)
+			return true;
+
+		try {
+			const extra = JSON.parse(value);
+			if (!extra || typeof extra !== 'object' || Array.isArray(extra))
+				return _('Expecting: %s').format(_('a JSON object'));
+		} catch(e) {
+			return _('Expecting: %s').format(_('a JSON object'));
+		}
+
+		return true;
+	}
+	o.depends('transport', 'xhttp');
+	o.modalonly = true;
+	/* XHTTP config end */
+
 	o = s.option(form.ListValue, 'packet_encoding', _('Packet encoding'));
 	o.value('', _('none'));
 	o.value('packetaddr', _('packet addr (v2ray-core v5+)'));
diff --git a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
index a75fe68..6d3f07e 100755
--- a/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
+++ b/root/etc/homeproxy/scripts/generate_client.uc
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ import { cursor } from 'uci';
 
 import {
 	getTime, isEmpty, parseURL, strToBool, strToInt, strToTime,
-	removeBlankAttrs, validation, HP_DIR, RUN_DIR
+	removeBlankAttrs, validation, singBoxHasXHTTP, HP_DIR, RUN_DIR
 } from 'homeproxy';
 
 const ubus = connect();
@@ -282,6 +282,256 @@ function generate_endpoint(node) {
 	return endpoint;
 }
 
+/* xhttp transport (sing-box-extended, podkop-engine) start */
+/* The settings of XHTTP as Xray writes them in the "extra" of a link, and
+ * their sing-box names. Ranges go as they are ("100-1000", "30", a number). */
+const xhttp_extra_keys = {
+	xPaddingBytes: 'x_padding_bytes',
+	xPaddingObfsMode: 'x_padding_obfs_mode',
+	xPaddingKey: 'x_padding_key',
+	xPaddingHeader: 'x_padding_header',
+	xPaddingPlacement: 'x_padding_placement',
+	xPaddingMethod: 'x_padding_method',
+	uplinkHTTPMethod: 'uplink_http_method',
+	sessionIDPlacement: 'session_placement',
+	sessionIDKey: 'session_key',
+	sessionIDTable: 'session_id_table',
+	sessionIDLength: 'session_id_length',
+	seqPlacement: 'seq_placement',
+	seqKey: 'seq_key',
+	uplinkDataPlacement: 'uplink_data_placement',
+	uplinkDataKey: 'uplink_data_key',
+	uplinkChunkSize: 'uplink_chunk_size',
+	noGRPCHeader: 'no_grpc_header',
+	noSSEHeader: 'no_sse_header',
+	scMaxEachPostBytes: 'sc_max_each_post_bytes',
+	scMinPostsIntervalMs: 'sc_min_posts_interval_ms',
+	scMaxBufferedPosts: 'sc_max_buffered_posts',
+	scStreamUpServerSecs: 'sc_stream_up_server_secs'
+};
+
+const xhttp_xmux_keys = {
+	maxConcurrency: 'max_concurrency',
+	maxConnections: 'max_connections',
+	cMaxReuseTimes: 'c_max_reuse_times',
+	hMaxRequestTimes: 'h_max_request_times',
+	hMaxReusableSecs: 'h_max_reusable_secs',
+	hKeepAlivePeriod: 'h_keep_alive_period'
+};
+
+/* Known but not for a client, or handled apart; anything else is reported */
+const xhttp_extra_skip = [ 'host', 'path', 'mode', 'headers', 'xmux', 'downloadSettings', 'extra',
+	'sessionPlacement', 'sessionKey', 'serverMaxHeaderBytes', 'scMaxConcurrentPosts', 'keepAlivePeriod' ];
+
+function xhttp_log(node, msg) {
+	warn(`${getTime()} [DAEMON] xhttp node "${node.label || node['.name']}": ${msg}\n`);
+}
+
+/* Zero is "the default" for every range of Xray's */
+function xhttp_range(v) {
+	return (v === null || v === '' || v === 0 || v === '0' || v === '0-0') ? null : v;
+}
+
+/* sing-box-extended refuses an empty or zero padding ("x_padding_bytes
+ * cannot be disabled"), the default of Xray is 100-1000. */
+function xhttp_padding(v) {
+	return xhttp_range(v) ?? '100-1000';
+}
+
+/* The check of Xray: an ASCII table, a length from 1, at least 2^31 IDs.
+ * sing-box-extended 2.7.3+ makes the same check and refuses the whole
+ * configuration, where a UUID would do as in Xray without a table. */
+const xhttp_session_tables = {
+	ALPHABET: 26, Alphabet: 52, BASE36: 36, Base62: 62, HEX: 16,
+	alphabet: 26, base36: 36, hex: 16, number: 10
+};
+
+function xhttp_session_table_ok(table, len) {
+	if (type(table) !== 'string')
+		return false;
+	for (let i = 0; i < length(table); i++)
+		if (ord(table, i) >= 0x80)
+			return false;
+
+	const m = match(`${len ?? ''}`, /^ *([0-9]+) *(- *([0-9]+))? *$/);
+	if (!m)
+		return false;
+	const from = int(m[1]), to = m[3] ? int(m[3]) : from;
+	const size = xhttp_session_tables[table] ?? length(table);
+	if (from <= 0 || size < 2)
+		return false;
+
+	for (let k = from, room = 0; k <= to; k++) {
+		let n = 1;
+		for (let i = 0; i < k && n < 2147483648; i++)
+			n *= size;
+		room += n;
+		if (room >= 2147483648)
+			return true;
+	}
+	return false;
+}
+
+function xhttp_base(node, extra) {
+	const t = {};
+
+	for (let k, v in extra) {
+		if (k in xhttp_extra_keys)
+			t[xhttp_extra_keys[k]] = match(k, /^(xPaddingBytes|sessionIDLength|uplinkChunkSize|sc)/) ? xhttp_range(v) : v;
+		else if (!(k in xhttp_extra_skip))
+			xhttp_log(node, `${k} is not supported and is ignored`);
+	}
+
+	/* Names of the session settings before Xray v26.6.22 */
+	t.session_placement ??= extra.sessionPlacement;
+	t.session_key ??= extra.sessionKey;
+
+	if (type(extra.headers) === 'object')
+		for (let k, v in extra.headers) {
+			/* sing-box refuses a Host among the headers, panels put it there */
+			if (lc(k) === 'host')
+				t.host ??= v;
+			else {
+				t.headers ??= {};
+				t.headers[k] = v;
+			}
+		}
+
+	if (type(extra.xmux) === 'object')
+		for (let k, v in extra.xmux)
+			if (k in xhttp_xmux_keys && xhttp_range(v) !== null) {
+				t.xmux ??= {};
+				t.xmux[xhttp_xmux_keys[k]] = v;
+			}
+
+	/* Without an xmux of its own Xray keeps up to 3 connections and reuses
+	 * them, sing-box-extended opens one for every request, and REALITY
+	 * servers may refuse such a flood. Take the defaults of Xray. */
+	t.xmux ??= {
+		max_connections: 3,
+		h_max_request_times: '600-900',
+		h_max_reusable_secs: '1800-3000'
+	};
+
+	/* Xray and sing-box-extended 2.7.3+ refuse both at once, and the whole
+	 * configuration with them */
+	if (t.xmux.max_connections && t.xmux.max_concurrency) {
+		xhttp_log(node, 'maxConcurrency cannot be used with maxConnections and is ignored');
+		delete t.xmux.max_concurrency;
+	}
+
+	if (t.session_id_table && !xhttp_session_table_ok(t.session_id_table, t.session_id_length)) {
+		xhttp_log(node, 'sessionIDTable or sessionIDLength is refused by Xray (an ASCII table, at least 2^31 IDs) and is ignored, a UUID is the session ID');
+		delete t.session_id_table;
+		delete t.session_id_length;
+	}
+
+	t.x_padding_bytes = xhttp_padding(t.x_padding_bytes);
+
+	return t;
+}
+
+/* "downloadSettings": a whole Xray stream with its own server, TLS or REALITY */
+function xhttp_download(node, stream, mode) {
+	if (type(stream) !== 'object')
+		return null;
+	if (!stream.address || !strToInt(stream.port)) {
+		xhttp_log(node, 'downloadSettings without address or port are ignored');
+		return null;
+	}
+	if (!(stream.network in [ null, '', 'xhttp', 'splithttp' ])) {
+		xhttp_log(node, `downloadSettings with network ${stream.network} are ignored`);
+		return null;
+	}
+
+	let settings = stream.xhttpSettings || stream.splithttpSettings || {};
+	if (type(settings.extra) === 'object')
+		settings = { ...settings.extra, host: settings.host, path: settings.path, mode: settings.mode };
+	if (mode === 'stream-one' || settings.mode === 'stream-one') {
+		xhttp_log(node, 'downloadSettings cannot be used with the stream-one mode and are ignored');
+		return null;
+	}
+
+	const dl = xhttp_base(node, settings);
+	dl.host = settings.host ?? dl.host;
+	dl.path = settings.path;
+	dl.server = stream.address;
+	dl.server_port = strToInt(stream.port);
+
+	if (stream.security === 'tls') {
+		const tls = stream.tlsSettings || {};
+		dl.tls = {
+			enabled: true,
+			server_name: tls.serverName,
+			insecure: (tls.allowInsecure === true) || null,
+			alpn: (type(tls.alpn) === 'string') ? split(tls.alpn, ',') : tls.alpn,
+			utls: tls.fingerprint ? { enabled: true, fingerprint: tls.fingerprint } : null
+		};
+	} else if (stream.security === 'reality') {
+		const reality = stream.realitySettings || {};
+		/* "password" is the name of the public key since Xray v25 */
+		const public_key = reality.password || reality.publicKey;
+		if (!public_key) {
+			xhttp_log(node, 'downloadSettings without a REALITY public key are ignored');
+			return null;
+		}
+		dl.tls = {
+			enabled: true,
+			server_name: reality.serverName,
+			utls: { enabled: true, fingerprint: reality.fingerprint || 'chrome' },
+			reality: { enabled: true, public_key: public_key, short_id: reality.shortId }
+		};
+	} else if (!(stream.security in [ null, '', 'none' ])) {
+		xhttp_log(node, `downloadSettings with security ${stream.security} are ignored`);
+		return null;
+	}
+
+	return dl;
+}
+
+function xhttp_transport(node) {
+	let extra = {};
+	if (!isEmpty(node.xhttp_extra)) {
+		try {
+			extra = json(node.xhttp_extra);
+		} catch (e) {
+			extra = null;
+		}
+		if (type(extra) !== 'object') {
+			xhttp_log(node, 'extra is not a JSON object and is ignored');
+			extra = {};
+		}
+	}
+
+	/* As in Xray, the host, the path and the mode of the node win over extra */
+	const t = xhttp_base(node, extra);
+	t.type = 'xhttp';
+	t.host = node.xhttp_host || extra.host || t.host;
+	t.path = node.http_path || extra.path;
